B.avc=s(["al-kahf","kahf"],t.s)
B.bol=new A.K(B.avc,"Surah Al-Kahf (18) is the surah many Muslims recite on Fridays, and memorising its opening verses is a widely taught practice. Open the Qur'an screen to read it, or ask a teacher about its virtues so that they can show you the sources.")
B.aMJ=s(["anxiety","anxious","worry","worried","stress","stressed","grief","dua for anxiety","dua for worry","dua for stress"],t.s)
B.bov=new A.K(B.aMJ,"\u0627\u0644\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0647\u064f\u0645\u064e\u0651 \u0625\u0650\u0646\u0650\u0651\u064a \u0623\u064e\u0639\u064f\u0648\u0630\u064f \u0628\u0650\u0643\u064e \u0645\u0650\u0646\u064e \u0627\u0644\u0652\u0647\u064e\u0645\u0650\u0651 \u0648\u064e\u0627\u0644\u0652\u062d\u064e\u0632\u064e\u0646\u0650 \u2014 \u201cO Allah, I seek refuge in You from worry and grief, from incapacity and laziness, from cowardice and miserliness, from the burden of debt and from being overpowered by men.\u201d (Sahih al-Bukhari 6369). You will also find it in your Morning Adhkar set.")
B.aJO=s(["witr","pray witr","how do i pray witr","how to pray witr"],t.s)
B.box=new A.K(B.aJO,"Witr is prayed after \u2018Isha until Fajr, as an odd number of rak'ahs \u2014 most simply one: the night prayer is two by two, and if dawn is near, one rak'ah makes it witr (Sahih al-Bukhari 990). The Prophet \ufdfa said Allah is single (witr) and loves what is single, and told the people of the Qur'an to pray witr (Sunan Abi Dawud 1416, sahih per al-Albani). He also taught al-Hasan ibn Ali a Qunut supplication for Witr that begins \u201cAllahumma ihdini fiman hadayt\u2026\u201d (Sunan Abi Dawud 1425, sahih per al-Albani). That report does not say whether it is said before or after ruku\u2018: ask a scholar of your madhhab.")
B.aEy=s(["morning adhkar","adhkar","dhikr","remembrance"],t.s)
B.bq8=new A.K(B.aEy,"Your Dhikr & Du'a screen holds the morning, evening, and after-prayer sets from Hisn al-Muslim with meanings. One report: whoever says a short \u201cIn the name of Allah\u2026\u201d formula three times in the morning is protected from sudden calamity until evening, and three times in the evening until morning (Sunan Abi Dawud 5088, sahih per al-Albani). Open it from Home and tap the counters as you recite.")
B.aFc=s(["ramadan","fasting","fast","sawm","siyam","roza","suhoor","iftar","ramadhan","ramzan","ramazan"],t.s)
B.bmP=new A.K(B.aFc,"Fasting Ramadan is the fourth pillar of Islam (Qur'an 2:183-185). \u201cWhoever fasts Ramadan out of faith and hope for reward, his past sins are forgiven.\u201d (Sahih al-Bukhari 38). Take suhoor \u2014 \u201cin suhoor there is blessing\u201d (Bukhari 1923) \u2014 and check the Islamic Calendar screen for this year's dates.")
B.aNc=s(["zakat","charity","sadaqah","almsgiving"],t.s)
B.bpl=new A.K(B.aNc,"Zakat is the third pillar \u2014 2.5% of qualifying wealth held a lunar year above the nisab. The Prophet \ufdfa told Mu'adh, when sending him to Yemen, that Allah has made charity obligatory on their wealth, taken from the rich and given to the poor (Sahih al-Bukhari 1395). The Zakat screen in Ar-Rayaan calculates it for you step by step.")
B.aCK=s(["prayer time","prayer times","salah times","namaz time"],t.s)
B.bnm=new A.K(B.aCK,"Your Prayer Times screen calculates today's schedule right on your device \u2014 tap GPS or choose your city, and turn on the bell next to any prayer to be alerted when its time arrives.\n[GO:/prayer]")
B.aB5=s(["how do i pray","how to pray","salah","salaat","salat","namaz","two rakah","pray two","pray 2","namaz ka tareeqa","namaz ka tariqa","namaz kaise","method of prayer","how to perform salah","steps of prayer"],t.s)
B.bny=new A.K(B.aB5,"Prayer is the second pillar. \u201cPray as you have seen me pray.\u201d (Sahih al-Bukhari 631). Five daily prayers are obligatory. A two-rak'ah prayer, in outline: make the intention, face the qibla and say Allahu Akbar, recite al-Fatihah and a surah, bow (ruku'), rise, prostrate (sujud), sit briefly and prostrate again. Stand for the second rak'ah and repeat it, then sit for the tashahhud and finish with the salam to the right and the left. Small details differ between the schools, so learn them from a teacher. The Huda guides in this app go step by step, and Shaykh Saqib Iqbal's channel (in Our Sources) teaches it beautifully.\n[GO:/huda]")
B.aCF=s(["quran","qur'an","koran","recite","recitation"],t.s)
B.bpX=new A.K(B.aCF,"The Qur'an screen holds all 114 surahs \u2014 tap any ayah to hear recitation by Shaykh Mishary Rashid Alafasy. \u201cThe best of you are those who learn the Qur'an and teach it.\u201d (Sahih al-Bukhari 5027).")
B.aHG=s(["du'a","dua","supplication"],t.s)
B.bpM=new A.K(B.aHG,"Du'a is worship itself (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 3372, sahih per Darussalam). For a need, begin with praise of Allah and salawat on the Prophet \ufdfa, then ask with certainty. Your Dhikr & Du'a screen carries the authentic daily supplications with their meanings.")
B.aEC=s(["eid"],t.s)
B.bmN=new A.K(B.aEC,"The two Eids are days of prayer, takbir, and celebration (Sahih al-Bukhari 950-956). Eid al-Fitr follows Ramadan; Eid al-Adha falls on 10 Dhul-Hijjah, the day after Arafah. Exact dates for this year are on the Islamic Calendar screen.")
B.aw1=s(["sources","authentic","hadith book","sihah","bukhari"],t.s)
B.boW=new A.K(B.aw1,"Ar-Rayaan builds only on the Qur'an and the Sihah Sitta \u2014 the six authentic books: Sahih al-Bukhari, Sahih Muslim, Sunan Abu Dawood, Jami' at-Tirmidhi, Sunan an-Nasa'i, and Sunan Ibn Majah \u2014 with Shaykh Muhammad Saqib Iqbal's channel for guided learning. See the full list on the Our Sources screen.")
B.aGi=s(["hajj","pilgrimage"],t.s)
B.boK=new A.K(B.aGi,"Hajj is the fifth pillar, owed once in a lifetime by those able (Qur'an 3:97). \u201cAn accepted Hajj has no reward but Paradise.\u201d (Sahih al-Bukhari 1773). Umrah can be performed any time of year.")
B.aMU=s(["tahajjud","night prayer","qiyam"],t.s)
B.bou=new A.K(B.aMU,"The night prayer is the best prayer after the obligatory ones (Sahih Muslim 1163). The last third of the night is a special time for du'a \u2014 your Prayer Times screen shows tonight's window.")
B.aua=s(["forgive","repent","tawbah","sin","same sin","keep sinning","sin again","sinning again","repeated sin","fall into sin","sin over and over"],t.s)
B.bq6=new A.K(B.aua,"Allah says: \u201cdo not despair of the mercy of Allah. Indeed, Allah forgives all sins.\u201d (Qur'an 39:53). The Prophet \ufdfa said: \u201cEvery son of Adam sins, and the best of sinners are those who repent.\u201d (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 2499, weak per Darussalam). The door is open \u2014 walk through it.")
B.aIA=s(["mother","father","parents"],t.s)
B.bpq=new A.K(B.aIA,"A man asked to go out and fight; the Prophet \ufdfa said: \u201cThen stay with her, for Paradise is beneath her feet.\u201d (Sunan an-Nasa'i 3104, sahih per Darussalam). The Prophet \ufdfa was asked who most deserves good companionship: \u201cYour mother\u201d \u2014 three times \u2014 \u201cthen your father.\u201d (Sahih al-Bukhari 5971).")
B.aGM=s(["istighfar","sayyid"],t.s)
B.bmn=new A.K(B.aGM,"Sayyid al-Istighfar is the master supplication for forgiveness \u2014 it opens your Morning Adhkar set. Whoever says it with conviction in the morning and dies that day enters Paradise (Sahih al-Bukhari 6306).")
B.aMA=s(["patience","sabr","hardship","difficult","trial","patience in the quran","patience in quran","what does allah say about patience"],t.s)
B.bot=new A.K(B.aMA,"\u201cIndeed, Allah is with the patient.\u201d (Qur'an 2:153). \u201cAmazing is the affair of the believer: all of it is good for him \u2014 gratitude in ease, patience in hardship.\u201d (Sahih Muslim 2999). This too shall pass, and nothing is wasted with Him.")
B.aEr=s(["name of allah","names of allah","99"],t.s)
B.bpA=new A.K(B.aEr,"\u201cAllah has ninety-nine names; whoever preserves them enters Paradise.\u201d (Sahih al-Bukhari 2736). Begin with Ar-Rahman \u2014 the Most Merciful \u2014 the name He opens His Book with.")
B.aBJ=s(["salaam","salam","assalamu","wa alaikum"],t.s)
B.bmu=new A.K(B.aBJ,"Wa alaikum as-salam wa rahmatullah - and upon you be peace and mercy. How may I walk beside you today? Ask me about worship, the Qur'an, this app, or simply talk.")
B.aCU=s(["how are you","how do you feel"],t.s)
B.bqm=new A.K(B.aCU,"Alhamdulillah - all praise belongs to Allah. More importantly: how are YOU? If something weighs on your heart, I can make du'a with you, or take you to Sakina for stillness.")
B.ap4=s(["who are you","your name","your hadi"],t.s)
B.bl2=new A.K(B.ap4,"I am Hadi - \"the guide\" - your companion inside Ar-Rayaan. I answer from the Qur'an and the Sihah Sitta: Sahih al-Bukhari, Sahih Muslim, Sunan Abu Dawood, Jami' at-Tirmidhi, Sunan an-Nasa'i, and Sunan Ibn Majah - and I know every room of this app. I would rather say \"I don't know\" than invent. My sister-teacher Wasia runs the letter school.")
B.aJd=s(["who is wasia","what is wasia"],t.s)
B.bpu=new A.K(B.aJd,"Wasia is the AI teacher of the Wasia Academy - the letter school built with love. She teaches the Arabic alphabet, reads with the child, and speaks in three voices: student, parent, and a Teachers' Corner for parents. Shall I take you there?\n[GO:/academy/gate]")
B.aLc=s(["thank","jazak","shukran","thanks"],t.s)
B.bnW=new A.K(B.aLc,"Wa iyyakum - and you likewise, many times over. May Allah accept from you. I am here whenever you need me.")
B.awQ=s(["what can you do","what do you do","features","guide me"],t.s)
B.boI=new A.K(B.awQ,"Three things, always: (1) answer from the Qur'an and the Sihah Sitta - verses, du'as, rulings, with sources; (2) teach you this app room by room - prayer times, Qur'an, stories, zakat, games; (3) walk you there myself - just say \"take me to...\" and I will. What shall we begin with?")
